    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠας</span></b> , τό, 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖας, οὖς,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ear,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sophr.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stud.Ital.</u>
				10.123
			</span></i>, cf. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.921
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤατα</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤασιν</span></b>  are cited by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—hence seems to be formed the fut.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠᾰτωθήσω</span></b> , 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκούσομαι</span>
			, Id., <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠατοθησῶ</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; 
				Dor.
			 word, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
